@project
Feature: bira project

  Background:
    Given I run "bira init --name test-project"

  @list
  Scenario: Project list shows initialized project
    When I run "bira project list"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "test-project"

  @json @list
  Scenario: Project list --json returns array
    When I run "bira project list --json"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "test-project"

  @show
  Scenario: Project show displays details of current project
    When I run "bira project show"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "test-project"
    And output contains "ID:"
    And output contains "Repo:"

  @json @show
  Scenario: Project show --json returns structured output
    When I run "bira project show --json"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output as JSON at path "$.name" equals "test-project"
    And output as JSON at path "$.id" exists

  @project-ref @show
  Scenario: Project show by explicit ID
    Given I run "bira project show --json"
    And I save JSON path "$.id" as $PID
    When I run "bira project show $PID"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "test-project"

  @delete @failure
  Scenario: Project delete requires --yes flag
    Given I run "bira project show --json"
    And I save JSON path "$.id" as $PID
    When I run "bira project delete $PID"
    Then exit code is not 0

  @delete
  Scenario: Project delete with --yes removes project
    Given I run "bira project show --json"
    And I save JSON path "$.id" as $PID
    When I run "bira project delete $PID --yes"
    Then exit code is 0
    And output contains "Deleted project"
    And output contains "test-project"
